{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Item profile and provenance (spec §5.1). validateProfile(profile) refuses an unknown key, a field object other than exactly {value, by, at, src}, a wrong type, an unknown src (local, import), kind or sensitivity, and a broken text rule (1..limit code points; no U+0000-001F, U+007F-009F, U+202A-202E, U+2066-2069, U+2028, U+2029) or list rule (1..32 items of 1..64 code points, no comma, no duplicate) with bad_request. checkProfileProvenance(prev, next, record, {self_device_id?}): prev is the validated profile at record.base_revision ({} for a create or a tombstone base), or null when not held (a create is always checked against {}). For each field of next: prev holds the key with an equal value (cjson of value) -> the field MUST be byte-identical to prev (same by, at, src); otherwise by MUST equal record.author and at MUST equal record.ts. A breaking field is dropped (dropped, key order); with prev null every field is kept. origins: a kept field shows its src only when by = self_device_id and (prev was held or record.author = self_device_id); otherwise \"sync\". cases MUST yield expect exactly. carry_forward: carryForwardMeta(meta) drops kind, item_ids, policy, profile and any key that, lowercased with \"_\", \"-\" and \".\" removed, equals a profile key with \"_\" removed; it MUST yield expect.",
